 ScenarioA;chunks;chunk;words_ok;dist_ok;result;base

⍝ In this scenario, we do simultaneous addition and searching of words.
⍝ As written, the shared WORDS/DIST are updated with no coordination, so threads corrupt one another and the scenario ERRORS partway.
⍝ Use )SIC to clear suspended threads.

 WORDS←''
 DIST←0 0⍴0

⍝ Reader/writer lock using the token pool
⍝ Only one writer at a time; writers block other readers and writers
⍝ Many readers may read at once if no writers are writing
 base←⎕TALLOC 1 'WORDSEARCH'
 RGATE←base+0.1   ⍝ Readers take +ve, writers take -ve
 READERS←0        ⍝ Track number of active readers
 WLOCK←base+0.2   ⍝ Prevent writers
                  ⍝ First reader takes this, last reader puts it back
                  ⍝ Writers hold this while writing
 ⎕TPUT WLOCK (-RGATE)

 chunks←(∊20⍴⊂40↑1)⊂CORPUS   ⍝ 20 chunks of 40 words each
 :For chunk :in chunks
     {}⎕TSYNC (AddWords&¨chunk),(Search&¨CORPUS[100?≢CORPUS])   ⍝ Many writers and readers
 :endfor

⍝ Check correctness
 words_ok←WORDS≡⍥{⍵[⍋⍵]}CORPUS
 dist_ok←(⍴DIST)≡2⍴≢WORDS
 result←'FAIL' 'PASS'⊃⍨⎕IO+words_ok∧dist_ok
 ⎕←'Words added: ',(⍕≢WORDS),'/',(⍕≢CORPUS)
 ⎕←'⍴DIST: ',⍕⍴DIST
 ⎕←'Scenario A: ',result
